1. stop_reason refusal finishes as content_filter; it read as stop.
2. The max_tokens RUN_ERROR carries the message_delta usage, so a reply cut
   off at the output ceiling still reports what it spent.
3. A stream with no stop reason ends in a RUN_ERROR (code
   incomplete-stream) instead of no terminal event, or a stop when
   message_stop arrives alone, and every RUN_ERROR carries the latest
   usage message_start or message_delta reported.
   Upstream PR to be opened for 1-3; remove when released.
4. The terminal event of a stop reason carries it as
   metadata.providerStopReason, so the service decides every stop reason from
   the SDK's union (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts) instead
   of reading an unhandled one as "stop". Remove when upstream exposes the
   raw reason.

